course: dictionary
lesson: 15677
title: Tidily: neat and in its place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tidily is an adverb. It tells you how something is done, so it often comes after a verb. If you do something tidily, you do it in a neat, orderly way, with everything in its proper place. «Please put your books away tidily.» The word away tells you where the books go, and tidily tells you how to put them there: neatly, with nothing left in a mess.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «Mia folded her jumper tidily and placed it in the drawer.» Folded and placed in the drawer are the clues. She did it carefully, so the jumper is neat. Ask yourself: would my meaning fit here? Neat fits, so you know you are right.
explain: Teachers often ask you to write and work tidily. «Set out your maths working tidily, one step under another.» Neat setting-out helps you spot mistakes, because you can see each line clearly. Tidily is about how a job is done, not only about how a room looks.
explain: Tidily can also be used informally in the UK to mean nicely and well enough. «The plan worked out tidily.» Here nobody is talking about neatness. It means the plan went well, without big problems. The same word can have two meanings, so the sentence around it tells you which one to pick.
fact: Tidily is an adverb: it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Tidily» means in a neat and orderly way, with everything in its proper place.
fact: «Tidily arranged» means set out neatly, so that everything is in order.
fact: «Put away tidily» means returned to its place neatly, so that nothing is left lying around.
fact: Informal UK use: «tidily» can mean nicely and well enough, as in «The plan worked out tidily.»
exercise: «Please put your pencils away tidily.» What does tidily mean? | Under the table | In a sad and slow way | *In a neat and orderly way | Very quickly and loudly
exercise: Your teacher says, «Write your spellings tidily.» What should you do? | Write on the back of the paper only | Write as quickly as you can, with no care at all | *Write neatly and clearly, with everything in its place | Write with your eyes closed
exercise: «The plan worked out tidily.» What does tidily mean here? | It was painted in bright colours | *It went well enough, without big problems | It was written in a notebook | It was very messy and untidy
test: «Hana dressed tidily for the school photo.» What does tidily mean? | Loudly, with a big smile | Quickly, in a hurry | *Neatly, with clothes smart and in order | Wearing her favourite pyjamas
test: «The books were stacked tidily on the shelf.» Which word is the best synonym for tidily here? | *Neatly | Carelessly | Messily | Loudly
exam: «Lee's report was written tidily.» What does tidily mean in this sentence? | Read aloud to the class | Drawn with paint | Scribbled in a rush | *Neatly and clearly, with everything in order
